    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>
    About the OurDNA Browser
  </h2>
  <div
    style={
      {
        "backgroundColor": "#f5f5f5",
        "borderLeft": "4px solid #0066cc",
        "borderRadius": "4px",
        "fontStyle": "italic",
        "margin": "0px 0",
        "padding": "20px",
      }
    }
  >
    <p>
      Please note that the OurDNA Browser is a resource intended for clinicians and researchers with formal training in genetics and genomics who understand the limitations of population genetic data. If you are part of one of our OurDNA communities and you would like to learn more about the program, please see the 
      <a
        className="c8"
        href="https://www.ourdna.org.au"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank"
      >
        OurDNA website.
      </a>
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>
    The 
    <a
      className="c8"
      href="https://www.ourdna.org.au"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      target="_blank"
    >
      OurDNA program
    </a>
     is led by the
     
    <a
      className="c8"
      href="https://populationgenomics.org.au"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      target="_blank"
    >
      Centre for Population Genomics
    </a>
    , a joint initiative of the
     
    <a
      className="c8"
      href="https://www.garvan.org.au/"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      target="_blank"
    >
      Garvan Institute of Medical Research
    </a>
     and the
     
    <a
      className="c8"
      href="https://www.mcri.edu.au/"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
      target="_blank"
    >
      Murdoch Children's Research Institute
    </a>
    , and is aiming to increase the genomic representation of multicultural communities. The goal is to fix a gap in genetic research: many Australian ancestry groups are not included right now, and we’re working to change that.
  </p>
  <p>
    The OurDNA program aims to harmonise and aggregate genetic variation data from over 20,000 Australians, including 8,000 new high-quality whole genome sequences from participants from genomically underrepresented groups recruited following participatory community engagement.
  </p>
  <p>
    The OurDNA Browser provides access to key summary statistics and allele frequency information from this dataset. Aggregate data download is currently under development: please check back for a release date.
  </p>
  <p>
    The OurDNA Browser is part of the
     
    <a
      className="-Link c7"
      href="/federated"
      onClick={[Function]}
    >
      federated gnomAD network
    </a>
    .
  </p>
  <h3>
